# Northampton Farm: "{1}, {T}: Exile target creature you own" - Bot2's Ornithopter is not Bot1's to target - and Bot1's
# Mutavault, a 2/2 creature until end of turn, is. In exile it is a land card, not a creature card (CR 400.7, 109.3), so
# when the Farm is sacrificed it is no "creature card exiled with this land" to return to the battlefield: it is one of
# "each other card exiled with this land", returned to its owner's hand (CR 607.2a).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mutavault
Northampton Farm
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Plains x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mutavault.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Northampton Farm.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Activate(Ability: becomes a 2/2)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Types = Land; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot1.Battlefield.Northampton Farm.Activate(Ability: Exile target; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Northampton Farm.Activate(Ability: Exile target; Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Exile = Mutavault
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Northampton Farm.Activate(Ability: Return)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire
Bot1.Hand = Mutavault; Plains; Plains; Plains
Bot1.Graveyard = Northampton Farm
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
